  "text": "Ébhlinne is an Irish mountain goddess. Her name also appears as Evlinn, Ébliu, Éblenn, and Eblinne. The goddess was honored in County Tipperary. That county lies near the border of County Limerick. Both counties sit in the southwest province of Munster. The Twelve Mountains of Ébhlinne carry her name. This range also bears the names Silvermine Mountains, Keeper Hills, and Slievefelim Mountains. Mauher Slieve is the highest peak of the range. This peak is the mother-mountain. Midsummer rites in her honor marked the feast of Lughnasa. These rites continued into recent times. ",
